1 paths hold a record whose shape decides its merge

  A line that depends on nothing — takes `merge=union`, because a reading depends on no other reading, so both sides may be kept
    (no path of this tree)

  One record for each entity, in a fixed order — takes `no merge attribute`, because two branches write two different lines, so an ordinary conflict is the correct report and no attribute is wanted
    (no path of this tree)

  A fold over those records / A fold over everything — takes `-merge`, because a fold depends on every record, so a merge keeps the current side and conflicts, and it is rewritten rather than reconciled. A clone that ran `headwater init --git --git-config` overrides it with `merge=headwater-regenerate` in `info/attributes`, which also agrees
    .headwater/taxonomy.lock — rerun with `headwater taxonomy resolve`

